cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, pipeline (FINDERS), or experimental benchmarks in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Lung Nodule Detection: A Hybrid, Explainable 3D Pipeline on LIDC-IDRI (FINDERS / HUSH)"
version: "1.0.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24375373"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
url: "https://github.com/Shrinkhal01/2026-lung-nodule-detection"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shrinkhal01/2026-lung-nodule-detection"
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "Shrinkhal"
    affiliation: "Central University of Karnataka"
abstract: >
  A reproducible, explainable 3D pulmonary nodule detection pipeline (FINDERS) evaluated on the LIDC-IDRI chest CT dataset. Combines multi-scale Laplacian of Gaussian (LoG) candidate nomination with a 5-seed 3D CNN ensemble operating on Hounsfield Unit (HU) and Hessian shape channels (HUSH: blobness and vesselness), validated via patient-level splits and occlusion explainability maps.
keywords:
  - lung nodule detection
  - 3D CNN
  - medical image analysis
  - chest CT
  - LIDC-IDRI
  - explainable AI
  - Hessian shape features
  - computer-aided detection
